The code statements that lead to the bug are:
devm_spi_register_controller(&pdev->dev, controller);
spi_controller_put(spicc->host);
Reason:
The probe function registers the controller with devm_spi_register_controller(), which automatically calls spi_controller_put() via devm cleanup on device removal. The explicit spi_controller_put() in remove() then causes a double-put (reference count underflow), leading to a potential use-after-free or other issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
// Remove the following line from meson_spicc_remove():
// spi_controller_put(spicc->host);
Reason:
Removing the explicit spi_controller_put() avoids the double-put because the devm cleanup mechanism already ensures the controller reference is properly dropped when the device is removed.

